  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "The points $A(5,3)$, $B(-17,-8)$ and $C(-6,-19)$ are joined to form a triangle. Prove that the triangle is isosceles.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$AB=AC=11\\sqrt5$, so the triangle is isosceles.\n\nThe distance formula gives two equal sides.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}AB^2&=(-17-5)^2+(-8-3)^2\\\\AB^2&=484+121=605\\\\AB&=11\\sqrt5\\\\AC^2&=(-6-5)^2+(-19-3)^2\\\\AC^2&=121+484=605\\\\AC&=11\\sqrt5\\\\BC^2&=(-6-(-17))^2+(-19-(-8))^2\\\\BC^2&=121+121=242\\\\BC&=11\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$\nSince $AB=AC$, triangle $ABC$ is isosceles.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
